# Snap package for the dsscp compiler. Rendered by packaging/render.py.
#
# CLASSIC confinement is required: a compiler reads source files and writes
# objects/executables at arbitrary paths, which strict confinement forbids.
# Classic snaps must pass a MANUAL Snap Store review before they can be
# published — factor that into the first release (see packaging/README.md).
#
# NOTE (scaffold): building a multi-arch snap from prebuilt tarballs is fiddly.
# This packages the linux-x64 tarball via the `dump` plugin; the arm64 arm is
# left to finalize when snap is enabled.
#
# The tarball is a PREFIX TREE produced by `cmake --install` (bin/, lib/, share/)
# — see cmake/DssInstall.cmake, the single owner of what ships. `dump` lays it
# down verbatim, which is exactly what is needed: `dsscp` locates its config tree
# by a path RELATIVE TO ITS OWN EXECUTABLE (../share/dsscp/<version>/
# dss-config) and its shared library by $ORIGIN/../lib, so nothing may be
# rearranged. That is why the former `organize:` remap of the exe is GONE rather
# than merely updated — moving the executable out from under share/ would leave a
# compiler that cannot resolve `#include <stdio.h>`.
name: @PKGNAME@
base: core22
version: '@VERSION@'
summary: '@SUMMARY@'
description: |
  DSS Code Prime (dsscp) is a config-driven, source/target/linker-agnostic
  C compiler. See @HOMEPAGE@.
grade: stable
confinement: classic
license: @LICENSE@

architectures:
  - build-on: amd64
    build-for: amd64

parts:
  dsscp:
    plugin: dump
    source: @URL_LINUX_X64@
    source-type: tar

apps:
  dsscp:
    command: bin/dsscp
